        "procedure": "A mixture of Gd2O3 (18.2 mg, 0.5 mmol), thiophene-3-carboxylic acid (3-TCA, 25.6 mg, 2 mmol), and H2O (10 mL) was stirred about 20 min, sealed in a 23 mL Teflon-lined autoclave, heated to 160 °C for 3 days, then slowly cooled to 20 °C in 12 h. Colorless crystals were separated mechanically from the gray powder and washed ultrasonically and repeatedly with ca. 10 mL mixed solvent (CH3OH:H2O = 5:5). The main text states that colorless crystals of 1 were obtained by hydrothermal reaction of Gd2O3 and 3-TCA at 160 °C, with hydroxyl groups generated in situ, but does not give reagent amounts.",
